            <ArticleTitle>Huge arteriovenous fistula between a giant aneurismal right coronary artery and coronary sinus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">012152/AIM.0015</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary arteriovenous fistulas are rare and may be congenital, traumatic, or iatrogenic. We report one of these rare congenital anomalies with a giant aneurismal right coronary artery (RCA) in a middle-aged lady who was asymptomatic for a long time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
